IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-documents-identity.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part X: sections 397 to 405 (falsification of books and documents, false prospectus, false billing,
-- identity theft and identity fraud, acknowledging an instrument in a false name). Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4.

§ `Part X -- sections 397 to 405`

§§ `Falsification of Books and Documents -- sections 397 to 402`

-- (1) Every person ... who, with intent to defraud, (a) destroys, mutilates, alters, falsifies or makes a false entry in a book, paper, writing, valuable security or document, or
-- (b) omits a material particular from, or alters a material particular in, a book, paper, writing, valuable security or document.
-- src:7346 | Falsification of Books and Documents
-- src:7347 | Books and documents
-- src:7348 | 397 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, with intent to defraud,
-- src:7349 | (a) destroys, mutilates, alters, falsifies or makes a false entry in a book, paper, writing, valuable security or document, or
-- src:7350 | (b) omits a material particular from, or alters a material particular in, a book, paper, writing, valuable security or document.
@ref s 397(1) (src:7346-7350)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a book, paper, writing or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the thing is, as a valuable security` IS A `s 2 valuable security kind`
      `the person destroys, mutilates, alters, falsifies or makes a false entry in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person omits a material particular from, or alters a material particular in, it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(1) the conduct is the offence of falsifying a book or document` MEANS
    IF `the person acts with intent to defraud` AND (`the person destroys, mutilates, alters, falsifies or makes a false entry in it` OR `the person omits a material particular from, or alters a material particular in, it`)   -- (a), (b)
    THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `the thing is a book, paper, writing or document`, `s 2 valuable security` `what the thing is, as a valuable security`)
         -- JUST FALSE when the thing is neither: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a book, paper, writing, valuable security or document"; NOTHING passes through from s 2 valuable security (NOTHING-kind (includes))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, with intent to defraud,"

@ref s 397(1) (the punishments) (src:7346-7350)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 397(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 397(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7346-7350)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 397(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7351 | Privy
-- src:7352 | (2) Every person who, with intent to defraud their creditors, is privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7353 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7354 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 397(2) (src:7351-7354)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to defraud their creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(2) the conduct is the offence of being privy to the falsifying of a book or document` MEANS
    IF `the person acts with intent to defraud their creditors` AND `the person is privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, with intent to defraud their creditors, is privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1)"

@ref s 397(2) (the punishments) (src:7351-7354)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 397(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 397(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7351-7354)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 397(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7355 | Falsifying employment record
-- src:7356 | 398 Every one who, with intent to deceive, falsifies an employment record by any means, including the punching of a time clock, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 398 (src:7355-7356)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to deceive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falsifies an employment record by any means, including the punching of a time clock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 398 the conduct is the offence of falsifying an employment record` MEANS
    IF `the person acts with intent to deceive` AND `the person falsifies an employment record by any means, including the punching of a time clock`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, with intent to deceive, falsifies an employment record by any means"

@ref s 398 (the punishments) (src:7355-7356)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 398 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 1: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 398 (the class of the offence) (src:7355-7356)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 398 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7357 | False return by public officer
-- src:7358 | 399 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, being entrusted with the receipt, custody or management of any part of the public revenues, knowingly furnishes a false statement or return of
-- src:7359 | (a) any sum of money collected by him or entrusted to his care, or
-- src:7360 | (b) any balance of money in his hands or under his control.
@ref s 399 (src:7357-7360)
GIVEN `the person is entrusted with the receipt, custody or management of any part of the public revenues` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly furnishes a false statement or return of any sum of money collected by them or entrusted to their care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly furnishes a false statement or return of any balance of money in their hands or under their control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399 the conduct is the offence of a false return by a public officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is entrusted with the receipt, custody or management of any part of the public revenues` AND (   `the person knowingly furnishes a false statement or return of any sum of money collected by them or entrusted to their care`   -- (a)
                                                                                                             OR `the person knowingly furnishes a false statement or return of any balance of money in their hands or under their control`)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, being entrusted with the receipt, custody or management of any part of the public revenues"

@ref s 399 (the punishments) (src:7357-7360)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 399 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 399 (the class of the offence) (src:7357-7360)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 399 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) In this section, company means a syndicate, body corporate or company, whether existing or proposed to be created.
-- src:7369 | Definition of company
-- src:7370 | (2) In this section, company means a syndicate, body corporate or company, whether existing or proposed to be created.
@ref s 400(2) (src:7369-7370)
GIVEN `the body is a syndicate, body corporate or company, whether existing or proposed to be created` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(2) the body is a company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a syndicate, body corporate or company, whether existing or proposed to be created`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "company means a syndicate, body corporate or company, whether existing or proposed to be created"

-- (1) Every person ... who makes, circulates or publishes a prospectus, a statement or an account, whether written or oral, that they know is false in a material particular, with intent
-- (a) to induce persons ... to become shareholders or partners in a company, (b) to deceive or defraud the members, shareholders or creditors ... of a company, or (c) to induce any person to (i) entrust or advance anything to a company, or (ii) enter into any security for the benefit of a company.
-- src:7361 | False prospectus, etc.
-- src:7362 | 400 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who makes, circulates or publishes a prospectus, a statement or an account, whether written or oral, that they know is false in a material particular, with intent
-- src:7363 | (a) to induce persons, whether ascertained or not, to become shareholders or partners in a company,
-- src:7364 | (b) to deceive or defraud the members, shareholders or creditors, whether ascertained or not, of a company, or
-- src:7365 | (c) to induce any person to
-- src:7366 | (i) entrust or advance anything to a company, or
-- src:7367 | (ii) enter into any security for the benefit of a company.
-- src:7368 | (d) [Repealed, 1994, c. 44, s. 26]
@ref s 400(1) (src:7361-7368)
GIVEN `the person makes, circulates or publishes a prospectus, a statement or an account, whether written or oral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows it is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body concerned is a company, by s 400(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to induce persons to become shareholders or partners in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to deceive or defraud the members, shareholders or creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to induce any person to entrust or advance anything to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to induce any person to enter into any security for the benefit of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 400(1) the conduct is the offence of making a false prospectus` MEANS
    IF    `the person makes, circulates or publishes a prospectus, a statement or an account, whether written or oral`
      AND `the person knows it is false in a material particular`
      AND (   `the intent is to induce persons to become shareholders or partners in the company`   -- (a)
           OR `the intent is to deceive or defraud the members, shareholders or creditors of the company`   -- (b)
           OR `the intent is to induce any person to entrust or advance anything to the company`   -- (c)(i)
           OR `the intent is to induce any person to enter into any security for the benefit of the company`)   -- (c)(ii)
    THEN `the body concerned is a company, by s 400(2)`   -- JUST TRUE when the body is a company; JUST FALSE (the "means" of subsection (2)) when it is not
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who makes, circulates or publishes a prospectus, a statement or an account, whether written or oral, that they know is false in a material particular"

@ref s 400(1) (the punishments) (src:7361-7368)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 400(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 400(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7361-7368)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 400(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- Paragraph (d) of subsection (1) is shown repealed.
-- src:7368 | (d) [Repealed, 1994, c. 44, s. 26]
@ref s 400(1)(d) (src:7368-7368)
`s 400(1)(d) as the text shows it` MEANS "(d) [Repealed, 1994, c. 44, s. 26]"

-- (1) Every one who, by means of a false or misleading representation, knowingly obtains or attempts to obtain the carriage of anything by any person into a country, province, district or other place,
-- whether or not within Canada, where the importation or transportation of it is, in the circumstances of the case, unlawful is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7371 | Obtaining carriage by false billing
-- src:7372 | 401 (1) Every one who, by means of a false or misleading representation, knowingly obtains or attempts to obtain the carriage of anything by any person into a country, province, district or other place, whether or not within Canada, where the importation or transportation of it is, in the circumstances of the case, unlawful is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 401(1) (src:7371-7372)
GIVEN `the person acts by means of a false or misleading representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly obtains or attempts to obtain the carriage of anything by any person into a country, province, district or other place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importation or transportation of it is, in the circumstances of the case, unlawful there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(1) the conduct is the offence of obtaining carriage by false billing` MEANS
    IF `the person acts by means of a false or misleading representation` AND `the person knowingly obtains or attempts to obtain the carriage of anything by any person into a country, province, district or other place` AND `the importation or transportation of it is, in the circumstances of the case, unlawful there`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, by means of a false or misleading representation, knowingly obtains or attempts to obtain the carriage of anything"

@ref s 401(1) (the punishments) (src:7371-7372)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 401(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 1: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 401(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7371-7372)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 401(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed, on such conviction, in addition to any punishment that is imposed,
-- is forfeited to Her Majesty and shall be disposed of as the court may direct. The forfeiture is an effect of the conviction; the direction of the disposal is the court's, a MAY with no consequence stated.
-- src:7373 | Forfeiture
-- src:7374 | (2) Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed, on such conviction, in addition to any punishment that is imposed, is forfeited to Her Majesty and shall be disposed of as the court may direct.
@ref s 401(2) (src:7373-7374)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(2) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1)` AND `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed"

DECLARE `s 401(2) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 401(2) direct how the forfeited thing is disposed of`

@ref s 401(2) (the court's direction) (src:7373-7374)
GIVEN `the thing is forfeited, by s 401(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 401(2) act of the court`
`s 401(2) the power of the court to direct the disposal` MEANS
    IF `the thing is forfeited, by s 401(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 401(2) direct how the forfeited thing is disposed of`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:7375 | 402 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 44]
@ref s 402 (src:7375-7375)
`s 402 as the text shows it` MEANS "402 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 44]"

§§ `Identity Theft and Identity Fraud -- sections 402.1 to 403`

-- 402.1 For the purposes of sections 402.2 and 403, identity information means any information -- including biological or physiological information -- of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with
-- other information to identify or purport to identify an individual, including a fingerprint, voice print, ... or password. "means" closes it; the purposes limit it (a scope with no "only": NOTHING outside it).
-- src:7377 | Identity Theft and Identity Fraud
-- src:7378 | Definition of identity information
-- src:7379 | 402.1 For the purposes of sections 402.2 and 403, identity information means any information — including biological or physiological information — of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual, including a fingerprint, voice print, retina image, iris image, DNA profile, name, address, date of birth, written signature, electronic signature, digital signature, user name, credit card number, debit card number, financial institution account number, passport number, Social Insurance Number, health insurance number, driver’s licence number or password.
@ref s 402.1 (src:7377-7379)
DECLARE `s 402.1 kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 402.1 a fingerprint`
    `s 402.1 a voice print`
    `s 402.1 a retina image`
    `s 402.1 an iris image`
    `s 402.1 a DNA profile`
    `s 402.1 a name`
    `s 402.1 an address`
    `s 402.1 a date of birth`
    `s 402.1 a written signature`
    `s 402.1 an electronic signature`
    `s 402.1 a digital signature`
    `s 402.1 a user name`
    `s 402.1 a credit card number`
    `s 402.1 a debit card number`
    `s 402.1 a financial institution account number`
    `s 402.1 a passport number`
    `s 402.1 a Social Insurance Number`
    `s 402.1 a health insurance number`
    `s 402.1 a driver’s licence number`
    `s 402.1 a password`
    `s 402.1 information of a kind not named in section 402.1`

@ref s 402.1 (src:7377-7379)
GIVEN `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `s 402.1 kind of information`
      `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402.1 the information is identity information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the section for whose purposes the question is asked` EQUALS 402.2 OR `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` EQUALS 403)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 402.2 and 403"
    ELSE IF NOT (kind EQUALS `s 402.1 information of a kind not named in section 402.1`)
         THEN JUST TRUE   -- the kinds the text names ("including a fingerprint, voice print, ... or password")
         ELSE IF `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "identity information means any information — including biological or physiological information — of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual"

-- (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2), an indictable offence referred to in either of those subsections includes an offence under any of the following sections: (a) section 57 ... (j) section 403 (identity fraud).
-- src:7384 | Clarification
-- src:7385 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2), an indictable offence referred to in either of those subsections includes an offence under any of the following sections:
-- src:7386 | (a) section 57 (forgery of or uttering forged passport);
-- src:7387 | (b) section 58 (fraudulent use of certificate of citizenship);
-- src:7388 | (c) section 130 (personating peace officer);
-- src:7389 | (d) section 131 (perjury);
-- src:7390 | (e) section 342 (theft, forgery, etc., of credit card);
-- src:7391 | (f) section 362 (false pretence or false statement);
-- src:7392 | (g) section 366 (forgery);
-- src:7393 | (h) section 368 (use, trafficking or possession of forged document);
-- src:7394 | (i) section 380 (fraud); and
-- src:7395 | (j) section 403 (identity fraud).
@ref s 402.2(3) (src:7384-7395)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402.2(3) the offence is one the subsection includes` MEANS
    IF    `the offence`'s section EQUALS 57
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 58
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 130
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 131
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 342
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 362
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 366
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 368
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 380
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 403
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes an offence under any of the following sections"; the list is not closed

-- (1) Every person commits an offence who obtains or possesses another person's identity information with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence.
-- src:7380 | Identity theft
-- src:7381 | 402.2 (1) Every person commits an offence who obtains or possesses another person’s identity information with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence.
@ref s 402.2(1) (src:7380-7381)
GIVEN `the person obtains or possesses another person’s identity information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is identity information, by s 402.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 402.2(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402.2(1) the conduct is the offence of identity theft` MEANS
    IF `the person obtains or possesses another person’s identity information` AND `the person acts with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the information is identity information, by s 402.1`, `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence`, `that offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 402.2(3)`))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who obtains or possesses another person’s identity information with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence"

-- (2) Everyone commits an offence who transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person's identity information, or has it in their possession for any of those purposes, knowing that or
-- being reckless as to whether the information will be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence.
-- src:7382 | Trafficking in identity information
-- src:7383 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person’s identity information, or has it in their possession for any of those purposes, knowing that or being reckless as to whether the information will be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence.
@ref s 402.2(2) (src:7382-7383)
GIVEN `the person transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person’s identity information, or has it in their possession for any of those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is identity information, by s 402.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the information will be used to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 402.2(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402.2(2) the conduct is the offence of trafficking in identity information` MEANS
    IF `the person transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person’s identity information, or has it in their possession for any of those purposes` AND `the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the information will be used to commit an indictable offence`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the information is identity information, by s 402.1`, `ccc13 any of` (LIST JUST `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence`, `that offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 402.2(3)`))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person’s identity information"

-- (4) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) or (2) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where
-- the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody. However, no proceeding in respect of the offence shall be commenced in a province without the consent of the Attorney General of that province if the offence is alleged to have been committed outside that province.
-- src:7396 | Jurisdiction
-- src:7397 | (4) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) or (2) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody. However, no proceeding in respect of the offence shall be commenced in a province without the consent of the Attorney General of that province if the offence is alleged to have been committed outside that province.
@ref s 402.2(4) (src:7396-7397)
DECLARE `s 402.2(4) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 402.2(4) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 402.2(4) the place where the accused is found`
    `s 402.2(4) the place where the accused is arrested`
    `s 402.2(4) the place where the accused is in custody`
    `s 402.2(4) a place that is none of those`

GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 402.2(4) place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402.2(4) the accused may be tried and punished by the court` MEANS
    IF `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence` AND NOT (place EQUALS `s 402.2(4) a place that is none of those`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody"

@ref s 402.2(4) (the bar) (src:7396-7397)
GIVEN `the offence is alleged to have been committed outside the province in which the proceeding is commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent of the Attorney General of that province has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402.2(4) the subsection bars the proceeding for want of the consent of the Attorney General of the province` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence is alleged to have been committed outside the province in which the proceeding is commenced`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the offence is alleged to have been committed outside that province"
    ELSE IF `the consent of the Attorney General of that province has been given`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the Attorney General of that province"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

