-- (1) Everyone commits an offence who fraudulently personates another person, living or dead, (a) with intent to gain advantage for themselves or another person; (b) with intent to obtain any property or an interest in any property;
-- (c) with intent to cause disadvantage to the person being personated or another person; or (d) with intent to avoid arrest or prosecution or to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice.
-- (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), personating a person includes pretending to be the person or using the person's identity information -- whether by itself or in combination with identity information pertaining to any person -- as if it pertains to the person using it.
-- src:7408 | Clarification
-- src:7409 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), personating a person includes pretending to be the person or using the person’s identity information — whether by itself or in combination with identity information pertaining to any person — as if it pertains to the person using it.
@ref s 403(2) (src:7408-7409)
GIVEN `the person pretends to be the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses the other person’s identity information, whether by itself or in combination with identity information pertaining to any person, as if it pertains to the person using it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(2) the conduct is personating a person` MEANS
    IF `the person pretends to be the other person` OR `the person uses the other person’s identity information, whether by itself or in combination with identity information pertaining to any person, as if it pertains to the person using it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "personating a person includes pretending to be the person or using the person’s identity information"

-- src:7402 | Identity fraud
-- src:7403 | 403 (1) Everyone commits an offence who fraudulently personates another person, living or dead,
-- src:7404 | (a) with intent to gain advantage for themselves or another person;
-- src:7405 | (b) with intent to obtain any property or an interest in any property;
-- src:7406 | (c) with intent to cause disadvantage to the person being personated or another person; or
-- src:7407 | (d) with intent to avoid arrest or prosecution or to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice.
@ref s 403(1) (src:7402-7407)
GIVEN `the person personates another person, living or dead, by s 403(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the personation is fraudulent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to gain advantage for themselves or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to obtain any property or an interest in any property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to cause disadvantage to the person being personated or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to avoid arrest or prosecution or to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(1) the conduct is the offence of identity fraud` MEANS
    IF `the personation is fraudulent` AND (   `the intent is to gain advantage for themselves or another person`   -- (a)
                                            OR `the intent is to obtain any property or an interest in any property`   -- (b)
                                            OR `the intent is to cause disadvantage to the person being personated or another person`   -- (c)
                                            OR `the intent is to avoid arrest or prosecution or to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice`)   -- (d)
    THEN `the person personates another person, living or dead, by s 403(2)`   -- JUST TRUE when personating; NOTHING when subsection (2) leaves it open
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who fraudulently personates another person, living or dead,"

