      `the person acknowledges, in the name of another person before a court or a judge or other person authorized to receive the acknowledgment, a recognizance, undertaking, release order, confession of judgment, consent to judgment or judgment, deed or other instrument or act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405 the conduct is the offence of acknowledging an instrument in a false name` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without lawful authority or excuse` AND `the person acknowledges, in the name of another person before a court or a judge or other person authorized to receive the acknowledgment, a recognizance, undertaking, release order, confession of judgment, consent to judgment or judgment, deed or other instrument or act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful authority or excuse, acknowledges, in the name of another person"

